### SYNTAX_ERROR ###
<feedback type="syntax_error">
  <header>COMPILATION FAILED: SYNTAX ERROR</header>
  
  <problem>Your code could not be parsed by the Prolog interpreter.</problem>
  
  <failed_code>
```prolog
{previous_code}
```
  </failed_code>
  
  <error_message>{prolog_error_message}</error_message>
  
  <common_fixes>
    <fix>Missing period at end of clause</fix>
    <fix>Clause split across multiple lines (MUST be single line)</fix>
    <fix>Singleton variable (use _ instead)</fix>
    <fix>Unbalanced parentheses</fix>
    <fix>Invalid predicate name (must start lowercase)</fix>
  </common_fixes>
  
  <output_format>
```prolog
% FIX: [What syntax error was corrected?]
your_corrected_rule(A) :- valid_body(A).
```
  </output_format>
</feedback>

